meta {
  name: Update Contact
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/contacts/{{contact_id}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body {
  {
    "name": "Jane Doe",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "phone": "+0987654321"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Update Contact

  Updates an existing contact. Partial updates are allowed - only provided fields will be updated.

  ## Authentication

  Requires Bearer token authentication. Only the contact owner can update it.

  ## URL Parameters

  - `id` (string): The contact's unique identifier

  ## Request Body

  All fields are optional for partial updates.

  - `name` (string, optional): The contact's full name
  - `email` (string, optional): The contact's email address
  - `phone` (string, optional): The contact's phone number

  ## Success Response (200 OK)

  ```json
  {
    "updatedContact": {
      "_id": "60d5ecb74b24c72b8c8b4567",
      "user_id": "60d5ecb74b24c72b8c8b4568",
      "name": "Jane Doe",
      "email": "jane@example.com",
      "phone": "+0987654321",
      "__v": 0
    },
    "message": "Contact updated successfully!"
  }
  ```

  ## Error Response (404 Not Found)

  When contact does not exist:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Contact not found"
  }
  ```

  ## Error Response (403 Forbidden)

  When trying to update another user's contact:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "You are forbidden from accessing another user's contact"
  }
  ```

  ## Error Response (401 Unauthorized)

  When authentication token is missing or invalid:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Please ensure to set the authorization header!"
  }
  ```
}